# UI and Design

## Colors

Use only semantic tokens (defined in [tailwind.config.cjs](tailwind.config.cjs)): `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-destructive`, etc.

- **Theme layering:** values come from the site's `site_<name>/theme.json` (or its `inherit_components_from` parent's), which overrides the fallback defaults in `client/src/index.css`. In section YAML, colors are theme IDs (`background: light-blue-5`), never raw CSS.

**NEVER use**: `bg-blue-500`, `text-red-600`, or `#...` in class names.

- Charts: `chart-1`…`chart-5`.
- Status: `status-online`, `status-away`, `status-busy`, `status-offline`.

## Component Library

shadcn/ui (new-york style). Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for class name merging.

### Toggle button bars

For compact single-select bars (filters, mode switches, section pickers), use [`ToggleButtonBar`](client/src/components/ui/toggle-button-bar.tsx) — not raw `TabsList` styling or `ToggleGroup`.

- **Standalone** (no panels): `ToggleButtonBar` + `ToggleButtonBarTrigger`
- **With `TabsContent` panels**: keep a `Tabs` root; use `ToggleButtonBarList` + `ToggleButtonBarTrigger` instead of `TabsList` / `TabsTrigger`

Visual contract: light muted track, grey border (`border-muted-foreground/20`), `text-xs` triggers, active = `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground`.

## Section Rendering

Section types map to components via [sectionRegistry.ts](client/src/components/sectionRegistry.ts): files in `client/src/components/{type}/variants/{PascalType}{Variant}.tsx` register automatically. [SectionRenderer](client/src/components/SectionRenderer.tsx) renders them; respect lazy vs eager loading.

- **Wrapper owns section background and vertical spacing:** `getSectionWrapperStyles` applies the section's `background`, `paddingY` and `marginY`. Components must not add outer `py-*` / `pt-*` / `pb-*` or paint `data.background`.
- **Icons:** Lucide via `getIcon(name)` from `@/lib/icons` (`"rocket"`); legacy `IconRocket`-style names still render. Fixed UI chrome may import from `lucide-react`.
- New components: follow [.agents/skills/internal-new-component/SKILL.md](.agents/skills/internal-new-component/SKILL.md).
